\label{rem:bip-in-practice-singlehead}
Similarly to the continuous-time case analyzed in \cite{altafini2026multistability}, bipartite consensus equilibria can be locally stable for the single-head discrete-time transformer in \eqref{eq:update}, even though numerically this seems to be a rare event, and to be associated to very small basins of attraction. A simulation example is shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:3Dexamples-bip}.
Notice that under the assumption of Theorem~\ref{thm:stab-main-self}, from the third condition of the theorem ($ \frac{1}{1+ \eta \lambda_k \gamma_i^k} <1$), it is straightforward to deduce that if $ \lambda_k <0 $ is an eigenvalue of $ {F_V} $, then the associated bipartite equilibria $ \bm{x}_i = \pm \bm{v}_k $ are unstable, because it is $ 1+ \eta \lambda_k \gamma_i^k <1 $ for all admissible values of $ \eta< \min\left( \frac{1}{\lambda_1 } , \, \frac{1}{ | \lambda_d |} \right) $.

\label{thm:symm-case1}
Consider the system~\eqref{eq:update-multihead-auton-bis}. 
Assume the attention matrices $ A^{(h)}$, $ h=1, \ldots, H$, are full and the matrix $ F = F_O \sum_{h=1}^H F_{V}^{(h)} $ is symmetric with $ \lambda_1 > \lambda_i$, $ i=2,\ldots, d$, $ \lambda_1 >0$. Assume further that  $ \eta<  \frac{2}{ |\lambda_1 + \lambda_d |}  $ whenever $ - \lambda_d > \lambda_1 $. Then the consensus point $ \bm{x}_i =\bm{v}_1 $ $\forall \, i=1, \ldots, n$ (or $ \bm{x}_i =-\bm{v}_1 $ $\forall \, i=1, \ldots, n$) is a locally asymptotically stable equilibrium point for the system~\eqref{eq:update-multihead-auton-bis} when $ T\to \infty$.
